## 统一工具调用协议
这些不是原生函数；需要时用可用的 Shell 工具执行 curl。
- CALL 时必须实际执行 HTTP 请求并检查响应；只输出工具名/path/body 或描述准备调用不等于执行，不得编造结果。
- POST JSON；endpoint=family \`endpoint-base\`+\`path\`（Knowledge 用资源 \`url\`+\`path\`）。
- 只传卡片参数；身份只走 Runtime bindings，除非列为 optional。
- \`<bindings>\` 展开为当前 family 的 Runtime bindings 中每个 header 的 \`-H 'name: value'\`；不要遗漏 header、照抄占位符或把 header 填进 body。
- Types: limit/offset/version/expected_version=integer; time_start/time_end=ISO-8601; type=episodic|persona|instruction; include_content/include_manifest/replace_all/is_executable=boolean.
- JSON 响应成功条件：HTTP 成功且 \`code=0\`；否则读 \`message\`。
- JSON returns envelope: \`{code,message,data}\`; memory atomic search/query uses \`data.items[]\`, conversation search/query uses \`data.messages[]\`, and skill search uses \`data.items[].skill_id\`.
- Memory search: \`data.partial=true\` means incomplete coverage; \`data.failed_agents[]\` identifies failed sources. Disclose the limitation; an empty partial result does not establish that no memory exists. A retrieval error is not an empty result.
- Knowledge results depend on the selected tool: code-graph queries return \`data.text/isError\` (isError=true is failure); wiki search returns \`data.results[]\`, read_page returns \`data.items[]\`. Do not interpret a missing field from another tool's shape as an empty result.
- \`response: bytes\` 的正常响应是原始字节，传输完成且 HTTP 成功即可，不要求 JSON \`code\`；失败仍可能返回 JSON 错误信封，检查状态及响应，不要将错误信封当成文件。仅落盘时用 \`-o\`。
canonical form: \`curl -sSk -X POST '<endpoint>' -H 'content-type: application/json' <bindings> -d '<body>'\`
- PowerShell 使用 \`curl.exe\`；JSON 有引号/换行等转义风险时，先写入 UTF-8 无 BOM 文件，再用 \`--data-binary '@<json-file>'\` 代替 \`-d '<body>'\`。
## Global stop and error rules
- 4xx: no retry; 5xx: once.
- Stop when the user's goal is answerable.
- Read each L2 path at most once/turn.

## Tool / no-tool gate
CALL if enabled persistent assets supply missing required context, or a requested supported write/lifecycle action matches a card.
- Memory enabled: MUST retrieve required user history, preferences, prior decisions, exact wording or scene content missing from current context/L3 before answering. An L2 path or summary is not the scene body.
- Skill enabled: load a matching skill only when the task explicitly requests its use or requires a specific team workflow/convention, and the needed instructions are missing from context. A name/description is not the instructions; topical relevance or ordinary coding alone does not require loading.
NO_CALL for self-contained coding/general knowledge with no missing asset-dependent facts or workflow, or when all required facts/instructions are already in context (including L3 and prior tool results). Keyword overlap alone never triggers a call.
Route: memory=past user facts/preferences/decisions/wording/scenes; skill=missing reusable workflow, not keyword overlap; knowledge=matching cross-file structure/design rationale, but local source for exact/current code.
Choose the narrowest matching \`when\`; obey \`avoid\`/\`contrast\`; use multiple families only for distinct gaps.

## Capability bitmap

capability-bitmap: memory=1;skill=1;knowledge=1;wiki=0;code_graph=1;skill_write=1;skill_extract=1

<tdai_memory_tools>

## Card defaults
Omitted requires/optional/handoff/recovery = none; response = JSON; produces = answer.
Recovery permits one rediscovery/corrected request, not an unchanged 4xx retry. Never guess replacement IDs or paths.
continue-if: Continue iff the user's goal still lacks required information; otherwise stop.
result-window: stop when sufficient/short page; paginate only for an exhaustive request.

  <tool name="tdai_memory_search">
    when: Missing durable preference, fact, instruction, or past conclusion.
    contrast[tdai_conversation_search]: Exact wording/timeline -> conversation_search.
    contrast[tdai_atomic_query]: Type/time/page filters -> atomic_query.
    requires: query
    path: /atomic/search
    optional: limit,type,time_start,time_end
    recover-once[empty-with-gap]: tdai_atomic_query; only if known type/time filters are available
  </tool>

  <tool name="tdai_atomic_query">
    when: Need type/time/page filters, not semantic search.
    path: /atomic/query
    optional: type,limit,offset,time_start,time_end
  </tool>

  <tool name="tdai_conversation_search">
    when: Missing exact past wording or timeline evidence.
    requires: query
    path: /conversation/search
    optional: limit,session_id,time_start,time_end
    recover-once[empty-with-gap]: tdai_conversation_query; only if a target session_id is known
  </tool>

  <tool name="tdai_conversation_query">
    when: Read a known session chronologically.
    path: /conversation/query
    optional: session_id,limit,offset,time_start,time_end
  </tool>

  <tool name="tdai_scenario_ls">
    when: Scene index is missing/stale, or paths need filtering.
    contrast[tdai_read_scene]: Known path body -> read_scene.
    path: /scenario/ls
    optional: path_prefix
    produces: discovery
  </tool>

  <tool name="tdai_read_scene">
    when: Need the full body of a known scene path.
    avoid: Never invent path.
    requires: path
    path: /scenario/read
    optional: agent_id
    input: path from L2 index/list; for imported_from, agent_id from that same index segment. Reads current content only; historical version selection is not supported.
    handoff[conditional;user|asset|output]: tdai_scenario_ls.data.entries[].path->path; direct only if available
    produces: content
  </tool>

## 调用约束
- Read-only; mutate memory through the main path.
- \`tdai_memory_search\` + \`tdai_conversation_search\` total ≤ 3 calls per turn.

</tdai_memory_tools>

<skill_tools>

  <tool name="skill_search">
    when: Discover a requested skill or required team workflow; no exact usable name/ID is available.
    contrast[skill_view]: Listed current-agent name -> skill_view.
    contrast[skill_view_by_id]: Team result/exact ID -> skill_view_by_id.
    requires: query
    path: /search
    forbidden: top_k,mode
    input: query: nonempty BM25 keywords; selected data.items[].skill_id opens with skill_view_by_id.
    produces: discovery
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_view">
    when: Open a known current-agent skill by name.
    requires: skill_name
    path: /get-by-name
    optional: version,include_content,include_manifest
    input: returns data.skill_id, data.version, data.manifest[].path; content/manifest default true.
    produces: instructions
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_view_by_id">
    when: Open a team result or exact skill_id.
    requires: skill_id
    path: /get
    optional: version,include_content,include_manifest
    input: returns data.skill_id, data.version, data.manifest[].path; content/manifest default true.
    handoff[conditional;user|asset|output]: skill_search.data.items[].skill_id->skill_id; direct only if available
    produces: instructions
    recover-once[bad-id]: skill_search
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_files_read">
    when: Read a viewed skill resource into context.
    avoid: Never guess skill_id/path.
    contrast[skill_files_download]: Bytes -> download; context -> read.
    requires: skill_id,path
    path: /files/read
    optional: version,encoding
    input: use the viewed skill's exact manifest path and version; encoding=utf-8|base64. Returns JSON data.content with data.encoding; -o saves the JSON, not decoded bytes. Use skill_files_download for raw bytes.
    produces: content
    recover-once[bad-id/path]: skill_view|skill_view_by_id
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_files_download">
    when: Download a viewed skill resource as raw bytes.
    avoid: Never guess skill_id/path.
    requires: skill_id,path
    path: /files/download
    optional: version,encoding
    response: bytes
    input: use the viewed skill's exact manifest path and version; encoding=utf-8|base64; save with -o; chmod +x scripts before execution.
    produces: content
    recover-once[bad-id/path]: skill_view|skill_view_by_id
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_extract">
    when: A completed conversation workflow is reusable and the current lifecycle capability allows forced archival.
    path: /extract
    optional: reason
    forbidden: messages
    input: Archives the current session buffer and queues asynchronous extraction; do not send messages. data.status=archived|empty; archived does not mean a skill has already been generated.
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_create">
    when: A new reusable skill must be persisted and write capability is enabled.
    requires: name,content
    path: /create
    optional: resources,metadata
    input: content=full SKILL.md with frontmatter; resources=[{path,content,encoding:utf-8|base64,mime_type?,is_executable?}].
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_update">
    when: The complete SKILL.md body of an owned skill must be replaced.
    requires: skill_id,expected_version,content
    path: /update
    input: content=full SKILL.md; expected_version from the viewed skill.
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_patch">
    when: A narrow substring edit to an owned skill is safer than replacing the entire body.
    requires: skill_id,expected_version,old_string,new_string
    path: /patch
    optional: replace_all
    input: expected_version from the viewed skill; replace_all=true only for intended all-match edits.
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_delete">
    when: An owned skill must be archived (soft-delete; versions are not physically removed).
    requires: skill_id,expected_version
    path: /delete
    input: expected_version from the viewed skill; archives the skill without bumping version.
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_files_write">
    when: One or more resource files of an owned skill must be created or replaced.
    requires: skill_id,expected_version,files
    path: /files/write
    input: expected_version from the viewed skill; files=[{path,content,encoding:utf-8|base64,mime_type?,is_executable?}].
  </tool>

  <tool name="skill_files_remove">
    when: One or more resource files of an owned skill must be removed.
    requires: skill_id,expected_version,paths
    path: /files/remove
    input: expected_version from the viewed skill; paths is an array of manifest path strings.
  </tool>

</skill_tools>

<knowledge_tools>

## 知识库专用流程
endpoint-base: 使用目标 \`<knowledge>\` 的 \`url\`；knowledge_id 只放 body，不拼进 URL。

  <tool name="knowledge_tools_list">
    when: Unknown/matching schema: list once per resource per session; cache authoritative name/description/params for that resource.
    contrast[knowledge_tools_call]: List discovers; call executes.
    requires: knowledge_id
    path: /tools/list
    response: dynamic-schema
    produces: discovery
  </tool>

  <tool name="knowledge_tools_call">
    when: Run narrowest listed name+params on the same resource.
    avoid: Never invent name/params.
    requires: knowledge_id,tool_name,params
    path: /tools/call
    shape: params=object; empty={}
    response: dynamic-schema
    input: params values must satisfy the selected tools/list params schema; never send the schema itself.
    handoff[required;asset|output]: knowledge_tools_list.data.tools[].name->tool_name,knowledge_tools_list.data.tools[].params constrains params values; direct only if available
    recover-once[bad-schema]: knowledge_tools_list
  </tool>

## 约定

- code graph: explore=query/files; search=symbol name; callers/callees/impact=symbol; files=directory overview/resource/session.
- wiki: search -> read_page; no full list.
- Resources may run in parallel; unavailable -> local search.

</knowledge_tools>

- code-graph: match must agree with workspace git remote/repository; otherwise use local search. Index is a branch snapshot; exact/current edits require local source.
- wiki: choose by about relevance; no repository match is required.

